<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bi Sheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1051</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bi Sheng was a Chinese artisan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> credited with inventing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/movable-type">movable type</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> using ceramic characters around 1040 CE. His method is recorded in the writings of the scholar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shen-kuo">Shen Kuo</a>. The invention predated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-gutenberg">Gutenberg</a>'s press by about four centuries and is counted among the major technological achievements of Song <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bi-sheng.jpg" alt="Bi Sheng" width="278" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Popolon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beijing.Musee_imprimerie.caracteres_mobiles.Bisheng.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
